		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Maximum number of objects.: 32k limit reached...]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=3955#p3955"><![CDATA[
Another limitation  was reached in btSequentialImpulseConstraintSolver.<br><div class="codebox"><p>Code: </p><pre><code>structbtOrderIndex{short intm_manifoldIndex; short intm_pointIndex;};#define SEQUENTIAL_IMPULSE_MAX_SOLVER_POINTS 16384static btOrderIndexgOrder[SEQUENTIAL_IMPULSE_MAX_SOLVER_POINTS];</code></pre></div>This code only allows up to 16384 but in some of my test this limit was reached with crash!<br><br>Also to make gOrder static seems to be not really thread safe for me.<br>Especially in some of my test I am using two or more Bullet instances simultaneous.<br><br>Edit:  SOLVER_CACHE_FRIENDLY seems to solve this problem becouse solveGroupCacheFriendly() function used instate with dynamic arrays.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=312">Remotion</a> — Mon Mar 19, 2007 6:16 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
